commit 09d34002298153ec51dcae233d4ca1d17f239210
Author: Marcus Schack Abildskov <work@marcus-sa.dev>
Date:   Sun Nov 22 05:35:19 2026 +0100

    feat(node-local-persistent-volume): attach the node-local volume as the second disk at launch
    
    The launch path owns the volume: it takes the single-writer claim (waiting up to 30 s), ensures the volume under the adapter-owned deadline, and attaches it as the second disk. The three volume invariants join the simulation catalogue.
    
    Two quint runs (no_space, store_absent) stay pending while a spec decision is made.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Step-Id: 04-02
    Task-Id: node-local-persistent-volume

